Article 4 (Standards for Preparation of Settlement Documents and Matters to Be Stated Therein, etc.) The standards for preparing settlement documents of a ship investment company under Article 38 of the Act, and matters to be stated therein, shall conform to the corporate accounting standards under Article 13 of the Act on External Audit of Stock Companies. However, the settlement documents shall be prepared so that distributions may be made up to the greater of (i) the amount obtained by adding the amounts under subparagraphs 1 through 5 to the net profit or loss for the current term stated in the company's settlement documents and deducting the amounts under subparagraphs 6 through 9, and (ii) profits available for dividends under the Commercial Act:
1. Depreciation expenses for tangible assets;
2. Foreign currency translation losses;
3. Expenses, other than those under subparagraphs 1 and 2, that reduce net income for the current term without a net cash outflow;
4. Amounts recovered from finance lease receivables;
5. Decreases in assets or increases in liabilities resulting from operating activities;
6. Amounts of principal repayments of borrowings;
7. Foreign currency translation gains;
8. Income, other than that under subparagraphs 6 and 7, that increases net income for the current term without a cash inflow;
9. Increases in assets or decreases in liabilities resulting from operating activities.
